{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"7279bbe7d04186675e0de888790aa9ff875ec2caa0084f33602c92941dfba8b8","packTokens":2643,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":417,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":608,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1298,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement and receiving data, and map PO lines to lots and pens with traceability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Forecast market dates and target weights from incoming animal data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, wastage, and multi-horizon projections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations from ingredients, calculating nutrition and cost.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level daily feed plans based on bunk rates, ration, and animal counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Log feeding activity, calculate variances and costs, decrement inventory, and roll up lot consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements as a time series.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate and update feed-to-gain metrics and projected ship dates from feeding and weight data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards and reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report with lot comparisons, filters, and CSV or PDF export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Create sample/mock data and a yard-level summary dashboard.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Deliver the proposed solution, architecture, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the feed-to-gain report and its exports follow the same yard and profitability access rules as dashboards?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Restrict report results and exports to the user's authorized yards and apply the same profitability restrictions as dashboards.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"How should users sign in to access operational records and role-based permissions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use email and password sign-in for the web app.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may import source records and change PO-to-lot and lot-to-pen mappings?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with operational access can import source records and change mappings; other users can view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may change target weights and growth-rate assumptions used for forecasts?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized managers can change the assumptions; other users can view forecasts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain inventory items, record receipts or adjustments, and change the wastage setting?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized inventory users may make these changes; operational users may view inventory and record feeding subject to stock controls.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may create, revise, optimize, and approve ration definitions?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only users with authorized ration-management access may perform these actions; other users may view rations.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should feed-plan creation or adjustment permissions differ from updating a plan's execution status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Authorized planners generate or adjust plans; operators may update execution status for their assigned pens.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may add weight measurements to a lot's history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Only authorized livestock or operations users may add measurements; other users may view them.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive feedlot web app with email-and-password authentication, permission-based navigation and actions, and session-expiry handling that clears protected data and returns users to sign-in.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide authorized users with mock procurement and receiving import, record previews and results, PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen allocation mapping, and repeat-import matching and allocation-conflict reporting; display existing records and mappings without enabled change actions to users lacking the relevant access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Display lot forecasts using incoming animal data and yard defaults, apply lot-specific overrides, show projected dates as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and restrict forecast-assumption editing to authorized managers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Display feed inventory, stock movements, and projections across daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons; let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts and adjustments, and edit wastage settings; distinguish actual wastage from delivered-feed consumption.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized ration managers create, revise, optimize, and approve rations; display ingredients, proportions, nutrition, and costs; and show the lowest-cost qualifying optimized mix separately from saved rations until explicitly saved.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized planners create and adjust dated pen-level feed plans, display returned plan details and execution status, flag plans for review when relevant inputs change, and preserve saved values until an authorized update or regeneration.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Allow assigned-pen operators to update plan execution status, show refusals for rejected updates, and display actual intake and variance without automatically changing saved plans; keep plan changes permission-controlled.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Let operational users record feeding activity by pen and lot, including per-lot allocations, and display returned variance, cost, energy, inventory consumption, status, and lot totals; handle insufficient-stock errors, permission-controlled corrections and voids, and uncertain save outcomes without duplicate submissions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Let authorized livestock or operations users add lot weight measurements and display time-ordered measurement histories and returned gain information; display lot feed-to-gain metrics and refresh them after feeding or weight records change.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Present explainable feeding-adjustment and sale-timing suggestions based on lot weight-gain trends, without changing plans or sale dates unless an authorized planner explicitly acts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Display dashboard measures for yard and lot performance, inventory, feeding, weight, cost, and energy, and let users select the measure used to rank best- and worst-performing lots.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability, with CSV exports of filtered results, plus a feed-to-gain report with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters and permission-controlled CSV or PDF exports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Restrict dashboards, reports, exports, and lot-profitability views to records and fields permitted for the signed-in user's authorized yards and current permissions; remove newly unauthorized data from view and subsequent exports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Provide authorized users with visibly designated sample data, duplicate-load handling, confirmation before reset or replacement, and permission-controlled sample-data actions; exclude sample records from operational dashboard, report, inventory-total, yard-summary, and export results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Display a yard summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost using returned aggregates, and mark missing metrics unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a delivery overview or presentation page with the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal overflow or page scrolling, and provide touch controls of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels on narrow screens.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}